Contract requirements:
1. Validate ALL registry entries eagerly (including unreachable) — currently: yes, it catalogs all registry entries, parses versions and requirements. That does validate eagerly. OK.
2. First-found selection rule: depth-first backtracking, FIFO discovery order, candidates tried highest-to-lowest satisfying ALL constraints collected so far. Backtrack to most recent choice; undo that choice's deps and constraints before trying another version. Already-selected names do not expand deps again.
3. No recursion (explicit frames) — it uses explicit frames. OK.
4. Must terminate without iteration cap — the current code has `if (++iterations > 4096) return null;` which wrongly returns null for long chains! Bug: long dependency chains of >4096 packages would incorrectly return null ("no solution"). Also termination should be guaranteed naturally.

